{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1478150-dragonfire-vs-armor","id":1478150,"title":"Dragonfire vs armor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-06T09:19:31-07:00","id":1478150,"title":"Dragonfire vs armor","content":"Hey guys!<br /> <br /> I playing a game with a Beast and got a question about dragonfire atavism vs armor on general.<br /> <br /> Armor works normal on supernatural attacks?<br /> <br /> When i looked on beast the primordial their say on one line it applies to all attacks, but on other line it says \u201cnormal attacks \u201c.<br /> <br /> What you guys thoughts about this armor works on dragonfire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T15:23:58-07:00","id":1478166,"title":"","content":"In general, armor works against attacks of supernatural origin.<br /> <br /> The question to ask isn't if the attack is &quot;supernatural&quot; or not, but if it makes sense for the power in question to be lessened by having something between you and the source of damage.<br /> <br /> In the case of Dragonfire? Yes, it makes sense for armor to apply. The more between you and burning the better. Though since Dragonfire can potentially ignite things, and a lot of modern armors that aren't designed specifically to be flame retardant are flammable, that can be a mixed bag if you're worried about diminishing the threat a Beast posses with that Atavaism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T18:20:22-07:00","id":1478177,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer, it make sense, i was confused since mage has special magic armors to mitigate that type of damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1478150-dragonfire-vs-armor?p=1478166#post1478166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, armor works against attacks of supernatural origin.<br /> <br /> The question to ask isn't if the attack is &amp;quot;supernatural&amp;quot; or not, but if it makes sense for the power in question to be lessened by having something between you and the source of damage.<br /> <br /> In the case of Dragonfire? Yes, it makes sense for armor to apply. The more between you and burning the better. Though since Dragonfire can potentially ignite things, and a lot of modern armors that aren't designed specifically to be flame retardant are flammable, that can be a mixed bag if you're worried about diminishing the threat a Beast posses with that Atavaism.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T07:52:19-07:00","id":1478210,"title":"","content":"The Fire section (pg 172 in Beast) specifically calls out that most armor does apply its rating against damage from fire, but only for a number of rounds equal to its rating. I think it\u2019s reasonable to extend this rule to damage from Dragonfire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}